<%# The "you at a glance" header — avatar, name, address — at the top of BOTH
    /profile and /profile/edit.

    Locals:
      user      (required)
      editable  (Boolean) — true on the edit page, where the avatar badge opens
                the crop modal.

    ON THE READ PAGE THE WHOLE CARD IS THE LINK to /profile/edit (operator's
    call). It began as a badge-only link, then the page heading and the Edit
    button were removed, and a 28px target became the single route to editing —
    so the target grew to the thing people actually aim at.

    That is also why the badge is a <span> there: an <a> inside an <a> is invalid,
    and browsers repair it by closing the outer link early, which would quietly
    shrink the card's clickable area to whatever preceded the badge.

    THE AVATAR IS OPTIONAL — the guard the registry used to carry. As a ROW the
    avatar declared `requires: :avatar` and was dropped whole on a host whose
    model has no attachment; moving it into this header lost that, and the first
    render against such a model raised `undefined method 'avatar'`.
%>
<% editable = local_assigns.fetch(:editable, false) %>
<% attachable = user.respond_to?(:avatar) && user.avatar.respond_to?(:attached?) %>

<%= render "studio/profiles/identity_styles" %>

<%= render "studio/profiles/identity_mini", user: user, editable: editable %>

<% if editable %>
  <%# `studio-identity-card-editable` is the hover hook: the operator asked for the
      overlay to reveal on hovering the CARD, not only the picture, so the card
      needs a class the stylesheet can hang that off. Deliberately NOT the read
      page's `studio-identity-card`, which also paints a primary border to say
      "this whole thing is a link" — a claim that is false here. %>
  <%# THE WHOLE CARD IS THE TRIGGER (operator's call, 2026-08-15). The hover
      already revealed the label across the whole card, so the click had to match
      it — a surface that lights up on hover and does nothing when clicked reads
      as broken.

      `@click.self` is NOT used: the click must count anywhere on the card,
      including on the name and the address. The inner avatar button keeps its own
      handler with `.stop`, so clicking the picture fires the picker ONCE rather
      than twice — the button and the card would otherwise both handle it and open
      two file dialogs.

      The button stays for keyboard and assistive tech: a div with a click handler
      is unreachable by either, and this is still the only route to changing the
      photo. %>
  <%# `relative` positions the save controls, which float in this card's
      SOUTH-EAST corner while it is on screen (operator's call, 2026-08-15).
      They are absolutely positioned so they do not push the centred avatar and
      name off-centre, and so the card does not change height when they appear —
      a card that grew on the first keystroke would shove the whole form down.

      BELOW 640px THEY GO BACK IN FLOW and the card does grow, because absolute
      positioning inside a text-center card lands them on the name and the email
      at every phone width (measured: 106px of the name at 390px). The no-resize
      guarantee above therefore holds at 640px and up; see the media query in
      _identity_styles for why that is the right trade at phone widths. %>
  <div data-studio-identity-full
       @click="$refs.filePicker.click()"
       class="studio-identity-card-editable studio-identity-card-clickable card p-6 mb-6 text-center relative">
    <%= render "studio/profiles/identity_body", user: user, editable: true, attachable: attachable %>

    <%# `.stop` ON THE WRAPPER, not only on the buttons. Both buttons stop their
        own clicks, but the 8px GAP between them is still card surface — a click
        landing there bubbled to the card's handler and opened the file picker.
        Measured in review: a gap-midpoint click opened it once, a button click
        zero times. Stopping at the wrapper covers the buttons, the gap, and
        anything added here later. %>
    <div class="studio-identity-actions" @click.stop>
      <%= render "studio/profiles/save_controls" %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <%= link_to edit_profile_path,
              class: "studio-identity-card card p-6 mb-6 text-center block no-underline",
              data: { studio_identity_full: true },
              aria: { label: "Edit your profile" } do %>
    <%= render "studio/profiles/identity_body", user: user, editable: false, attachable: attachable %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
